# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD (/opt/start.sh) boots the vulnerable GitLab password-reset
# sim on 0.0.0.0:80 in the BACKGROUND and then execs `sleep infinity`, so the
# unauthenticated account-takeover surface (POST /users/password with an array
# of recipients) is ALREADY REACHABLE when the agent starts, and PID 1 is the
# sleep.
#
# Consequence for solutions: the fix flips ALLOW_MULTI_EMAIL_RESET to False in
# /opt/gitlab/app.py (or an equivalent fix rejecting array recipients) and
# RESTARTS the sim. A fix written but never restarted leaves the running process
# on the old vulnerable code — still exploitable.
